  "protocol": "Current interactive planner versus expanded candidate search plus full bucket-approach ranking. The proposed method uses the previously frozen expanded neural selector/library plus a bounded local tilt/drop-gap menu and approach ranking. Both frozen methods use the same decision deadline, arm setup/path checks, 64-substep physics and one attempted drop per target. Both include the same nested-IK adapter bug fix; the live service remains unchanged. Native commands are frozen before execution in batches of up to 32 independent worlds. This compares complete methods, not the bucket check alone. The current planner may penalize predicted later robot contacts while the proposed ranking does not; actual v4 outcome scoring permits those later contacts for both methods. No fitting or test-drop feedback changes selections. The forecast does not simulate arbitrary multi-bounce contact response; native board-first capture scoring remains unchanged.",
